 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Just had a new induction hob fitted, Beko. When I put my saucepan on it just flashes a U and doesn't heat. Is it faulty? It's brand new!!"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "A flashing 'U' on Beko induction hobs typically means the hob cannot detect a suitable pan. This is often due to the cookware rather than a fault with the new appliance. Induction hobs only heat magnetic pans (usually stainless steel or cast iron) that are flat and large enough to cover the heating zone. Please check if your saucepan has a magnet sticking firmly to its base, and ensure it is not too small for the zone. If you have another pan known to work on induction, try that one. Let me know what happens."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I tried a magnet: it doesn't stick to my saucepans (they're aluminium), but it does stick to my cast-iron casserole, and that one heated fine! So is the hob okay then?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, the hob is perfectly fine. The flashing 'U' code confirms it is working correctly by refusing to heat your aluminium saucepans, which are not magnetic and therefore incompatible with induction technology. Since your cast-iron casserole worked as expected, there is no fault with the appliance itself. You will need to use cookware that has a flat base and is magnetic (like cast iron or certain stainless steels) for this hob."
  }
 ],
